+# Code Correction and Optimization Plan
+
+Before applying major changes, we will "correct" the current codebase by improving its architecture, removing redundancies, and following Android best practices. This will make the application more stable, readable, and easier to extend.
+
+## User Review Required
+
+> [!IMPORTANT]
+> **Architecture Shift**: I propose moving logic out of Composables into **ViewModels**. This will separate "how things look" from "how things work".
+> **Redundancy Cleanup**: Currently, the app polls for data in multiple places (MainContainer, Dashboard, and WorkManager). I will centralize this so that only one process manages data updates.
+
+## Open Questions
+- What are the **"Big Changes"** you plan to apply next? Knowing this helps me prepare the architecture specifically for those needs.
+- Do you want to keep the 15-second polling as a fallback for FCM, or should we reduce its frequency to save battery?
+
+## Proposed Changes
+
+### 1. Architectural Improvements (MVVM)
+Currently, `DashboardScreen` and `MainContainer` handle network calls and polling internally.
+- **[NEW] DashboardViewModel.kt**: Move dashboard data fetching, polling, and attendance logic here.
+- **[NEW] MainViewModel.kt**: Move top-level navigation state and shared session logic here.
+- **[MODIFY] DashboardScreen.kt**: Update to observe state from the ViewModel.
+- **[MODIFY] MainContainer.kt**: Simplify by removing internal polling.
+
+### 2. Redundancy and Optimization
+- **Centralize Polling**: Ensure only the active screen or a background worker is polling, never both at high frequency.
+- **FCM Priority**: Rely primarily on FCM for instant notifications.
+- **Resource Management**: Move hardcoded strings to `strings.xml` and colors to `Color.kt` for easier theming.
+
+### 3. UI Cleanup
+- **[MODIFY] DashboardScreen.kt**: Break down large Composables into smaller, reusable components (e.g., `QuickActions`, `StatsGrid`).
+- **[MODIFY] MainContainer.kt**: Refactor the `NavHost` and `Drawer` logic for better readability.
+
+### 4. Dependency and Build Cleanup
+- Check for any unused imports or redundant dependencies in `build.gradle.kts`.
+
+## Verification Plan
+
+### Automated Tests
+- I will perform a `gradle build` to ensure no regressions are introduced.
+- I will use `analyze_file` to verify the new architecture is free of common errors.
+
+### Manual Verification
+- Verify that notifications still arrive via FCM and fallback polling.
+- Verify that the app handles configuration changes (like rotation or theme switching) correctly now that state is in ViewModels.
+- Ensure the UI remains responsive and looks the same as before.
